      "id": "01",
      "title": "From submit to done",
      "question": "Sketch a distributed task scheduler. What happens from submit to done?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "Task scheduler, question one. Sketch a distributed task scheduler, and walk a task from submit to done. Pause and sketch it out.",
          "pauseAfter": 4,
          "props": {
            "question": "Walk one task from <em>submit</em> to <em>done</em>."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "A client submits a task to one of the stateless API servers. It validates the request, puts the task on the queue, and records it in the state store as pending. The leader scheduler dequeues it, and checks the state store for a worker with enough free CPU, memory or GPU. It assigns the task, and marks it scheduled. The worker runs it, and reports running, then completed or failed, back to the scheduler, which updates the state store.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Queue, schedule, <em>run</em>, record",
            "nodes": [
