    {
      "id": "03",
      "title": "A highly available scheduler",
      "question": "The scheduler is a single point of failure. How do you make it highly available?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "Question three. The scheduler looks like a single point of failure. How do you make it highly available, without two schedulers fighting? Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "How do you make the scheduler <em>highly available</em>?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "Run several scheduler instances, but let only one act. Each holds a session with ZooKeeper or etcd, and races to create the same leader key. S1 won, so only S1 schedules. S2 and S3 stand by, watching the key. When S1 crashes, its session expires, and the key is deleted. The watches fire, and S2 grabs the key, as leader in a new epoch. It rebuilds its view from the state store, and resumes scheduling. And if S1 comes back still thinking it leads, its writes carry the old epoch, and are rejected.",
          "props": {
            "title": "One leader, <em>hot standbys</em>",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "zk",
                "label": "ZooKeeper / etcd",
                "x": 640,
                "y": 270,
                "w": 320,
                "h": 70
              },
              {
                "id": "S1",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 490,
                "w": 170,
                "h": 64
              },
              {
                "id": "S2",
                "x": 640,
                "y": 490,
                "w": 170,
                "h": 64
              },
              {
                "id": "S3",
                "x": 1000,
                "y": 490,
                "w": 170,
                "h": 64
              },
              {
                "id": "store",
                "label": "State store",
                "x": 640,
                "y": 680,
                "w": 240,
                "h": 60,
                "hidden": true
              }
            ],
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "S1",
                "to": "zk"
              },
              {
                "from": "S2",
                "to": "zk"
              },
              {
                "from": "S3",
                "to": "zk"
              }
            ],
            "panels": [
              {
                "key": "lock",
                "label": "/scheduler/leader",
                "type": "list",
                "initial": [
                  "(free)"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "steps": [
              {
                "at": "races",
                "edges": {
                  "S1-zk": "relax",
                  "S2-zk": "relax",
                  "S3-zk": "relax"
                },
                "note": "All three race to create the leader key"
              },
              {
                "at": "won",
                "nodes": {
                  "S1": "active"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "S1-zk": "tree",
                  "S2-zk": "base",
                  "S3-zk": "base"
                },
                "panels": {
                  "lock": [
                    "S1 · epoch 7"
                  ]
                },
                "note": "S1 holds the key: only S1 schedules"
              },
              {
                "at": "watching",
                "nodes": {
                  "S2": "queued",
                  "S3": "queued"
                },
                "note": "S2 and S3 stand by, watching the key"
              },
              {
                "at": "crashes",
                "nodes": {
                  "S1": "dim"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "S1-zk": "dim"
                },
                "note": "S1 crashes…"
              },
              {
                "at": "expires",
                "panels": {
                  "lock": [
                    "(deleted)"
                  ]
                },
                "note": "…its session expires, the key is deleted"
              },
              {
                "at": "grabs",
                "nodes": {
                  "S2": "active",
                  "S3": "base"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "S2-zk": "tree"
                },
                "panels": {
                  "lock": [
                    "S2 · epoch 8"
                  ]
                },
                "note": "Watch fires: S2 takes the key in epoch 8"
              },
              {
                "at": "rebuilds",
                "show": [
                  "store"
                ],
                "add": [
                  {
                    "from": "S2",
                    "to": "store",
                    "w": "reload"
                  }
                ],
                "edges": {
                  "S2-store": "relax"
                },
                "note": "Rebuild state from the store, resume"
              },
              {
                "at": "thinking",
                "nodes": {
                  "S1": "queued"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "S2-store": "base"
                },
                "note": "Old S1 is back, still thinks it leads…"
              },
              {
                "at": "rejected",
                "nodes": {
                  "S1": "dim"
                },
                "note": "…its epoch-7 writes are rejected (fencing)"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "recap",
          "say": "To recap. Stateless API servers, and a queue that absorbs bursts. One leader scheduler matches tasks to workers with room, and workers usually pull. Missed heartbeats mark a worker dead, and its tasks are rescheduled, so tasks must be idempotent. And leader election with epochs keeps exactly one scheduler in charge.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Task scheduler, <em>in four lines</em>",
            "items": [
              {
                "at": "absorbs",
                "text": "Stateless API servers; a queue absorbs bursts.",
                "code": "pending"
              },
              {
                "at": "matches",
                "text": "One leader matches tasks to workers with room.",
                "code": "pull-based"
              },
              {
                "at": "rescheduled",
                "text": "Missed heartbeats → reschedule; be idempotent.",
                "code": "at-least-once"
              },
              {
                "at": "epochs",
                "text": "Election + epochs: exactly one scheduler.",
                "code": "fencing"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
